  "ordinal": 0,
  "summary": "The Stock Story\nJust when some were beginning to think the tanker market had begun its decline, spot market rates have rebounded across all markets. In particular, rates in the Atlantic Basin have been at the famed \"fourth quarter 2004\" for a couple of weeks. In our Tanker Opinion, \"The Knife Edge\", we addressed the lack of VLCC availability in the Arabian Gulf that sparked the jump in rates, but the longevity of such a rally is really defined by market fundamentals.",
